// Title: Launch-VsDevShell.PS1 Proxy Execution
// Sigma ID: 45d3a03d-f441-458c-8883-df101a3bb146
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-19 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1216.001
// Description: Detects the use of the 'Launch-VsDevShell.ps1' Microsoft signed script to execute commands.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of the script by a developer
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/nas_bench/status/1535981653239255040
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_launch_vsdevshell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "Launch-VsDevShell.ps1" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "VsWherePath " or ProcessCommandLine contains "VsInstallationPath ")
